# 1. Project Context & High-Level Purpose
> **AI Context Requirement:** When creating or updating `README.md` or major project summaries, clearly articulate:
> 1. What problem the application solves and its core value proposition.
> 2. Primary target audience and major user-facing capabilities.
> 3. Production architecture and tech stack choices.

---

# 2. Autonomous Workflow Execution Order
Whenever executing a feature implementation or major refactor inside VS Code, follow this **4-step lifecycle**:

1. **Establish context:** Read the relevant project plan, requirements, backlog, and applicable rules before deciding on an implementation.
2. **Inspect and plan:** Review the existing implementation and related tests. Identify the acceptance criteria, affected files, and a concise implementation sequence before editing.
3. **Implement and record:** Make focused changes that follow existing patterns. Add comments only to explain non-obvious reasoning. Keep project-status and completed-work documentation accurate as the work progresses.
4. **Verify and synchronize:** Run the smallest relevant checks, confirm the acceptance criteria, update the README when project setup or architecture changes, and report the outcome and any remaining limitations.
